# Reuse before creating (course / curriculum / AI)

Before **any new REST path**, Flask route, AI client, or duplicate fetch: search existing APIs, fill the template, then reuse or extend. Do not add a sibling resource because a feature needs similar data.

## Investigation template (required in the plan or PR notes)

```text
Existing Endpoint:
<endpoint>

Purpose:
<what it currently does>

Required Data:
<what the new feature needs>

Can Reuse:
YES / NO

If YES:
<how it will be reused/extended>

If NO:
<why an existing endpoint cannot reasonably support the requirement>
```

Cover services, repositories, models, DTOs, auth, caching, and generated-content patterns — not only the controller.

## Decision order

```text
Existing endpoint → satisfies need? YES → Reuse
                                 NO → safe to extend? YES → Extend
                                                   NO → new endpoint only
```

A new endpoint is allowed only when no existing one provides the data **and** extending it would break the contract (auth, payload size, or a different resource). Persist through existing CRUD even if a new LLM draft route is justified.

## Locked reuse map (Skillama)

There is **no Lesson entity**. Course = `courses`; Module = `course_curricula` document; lecture/topic = nested `Submodule`.

| Need | Reuse | Do not create |
|------|-------|----------------|
| Title, description, thumbnail, flags | `GET /skillama/courses/{id}` | Combined course+curriculum GET; do not put modules on Course |
| Module + lecture tree, scripts, order | `GET /skillama/courses/{courseId}/curriculum` (`guest=true`, `forAdmin=true`) | `GET .../modules`, `.../lessons`, a second curriculum GET |
| Single module | `GET /skillama/curriculum/{moduleId}` | New module resource |
| Structure writes | `/skillama/curriculum/module` and `.../submodule/{idx}` (`idx` is array index) | Parallel CRUD |
| Locks / progress | `GET /skillama/user-profile/access-control?courseId=` | Lock flags on curriculum GET |
| Lecture narration | `POST /skillama/lecture/generate` → Flask `/generate_lecture` via `SkillamaAiClient` | New LLM client or Java proxy |
| Quiz / chat / code / images | Existing `SkillamaAiClient` + Flask `/generate_quiz`, `/handle_query`, `/generate_code`, `/generate_output`, `/generate_image` | Second AI HTTP stack |

LMS already composes course + curriculum + access-control on load (`src/app/lms/(main)/page.js`, `src/utils/switchLmsCourse.js`). Curriculum cache: RTK `getCourseCurriculum`.

Do **not** revive unused legacy `/api/public/course/{courseId}/curriculum`.

**True gap today:** no bulk “generate entire curriculum from a prompt.” A new Flask **draft** route is the only plausible new path; commit still uses existing curriculum CRUD. Do not add a persist API for that.

Optional `GET /courses/{id}?include=curriculum` is an extension of last resort, only after a measured round-trip problem — not a new resource.
